.TH AWCC-LUX-DASHBOARD 1 "October 2026" "AWCC Linux 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
awcc-lux-dashboard \- Cybernetic TrueColor Telemetry Cockpit for AWCC Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awcc-lux-dashboard.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B awcc-lux-dashboard.py
is an interactive, responsive terminal cockpit featuring cinema-grade 24-bit TrueColor
color grading, smooth thermal gradients, dynamic terminal geometry adaptation, and real-time
telemetry tracking.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.B 1\(en6
Instantly switch performance profiles (1: Battery, 2: Quiet, 3: Balance, 4: Mid, 5: High, 6: Ultra).
.TP
.B F9, G
Toggle Game Shift (G-Mode) instantaneous cooling turbine overboost.
.TP
.B C, T
Cycle visual themes (Cryo-Tech Pro, Cyberpunk 2077, Dark Core OLED, Solar Flare, Matrix Emerald, Vaporwave Sunset).
.TP
.B Q, Esc, Ctrl+C
Cleanly restore terminal attributes and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-theme <\fINAME\fR>
Launch directly using the specified color theme.
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot, \-s
Render a single frame snapshot and exit immediately (useful for scripts and fast checks).
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Print help message and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR awccctl (1),
.BR awcc-mode (1)
